# Teferi's Reproach in a three-player game: "Choose target opponent ... All nonland permanents they control phase
# out." Bot1 has two opponents - Bot2 and Bot3 - and names Bot3 (turn 4). Bot3's Mox Ruby and Brazen Borrower phase out
# and their Tundra stays; Bot2's and Bot1's permanents do not, and Bot2's life is still changeable and Bot2 still
# targetable: Bot1's Lightning Bolt is refused at Bot3 - protected from everything - and the same action is accepted at
# Bot2 (CR 702.16b, 702.16j). The effects last "until that player's next turn" (CR 611.2a), which for Bot3 is turn 6,
# not the end of turn 4 and not the caster's next turn (turn 7): on turn 5 (Bot2's) Bot3 is still protected - Bolt
# refused - and its life total still can't change when Bot2's Cauldron Familiar makes each opponent lose 1 life (Bot1
# does lose it, the control); on turn 6, once Bot3's turn has begun and its permanents phased in, the same Bolt is
# accepted and Bot3's life drops.

